{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A test that waits on a real setTimeout is racing the CI runner's actual load, not just your code — that's why it passes locally and flakes in CI.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Fake timers (vi.useFakeTimers / jest.useFakeTimers) let a test advance a controlled clock synchronously instead of waiting on wall-clock time.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Fake timers only fix flakiness caused by timer races specifically — unrelated flake sources (network, unflushed microtasks, layout timing) need their own fix.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
